Third-party parts. None of them is included in this repository. The scripts in tools/ download them when they are needed.

Musashi, a 68000 to 68040 emulator in C, by Karl Stenerud (github.com/kstenerud/Musashi). MIT license: Copyright 1998-2002
Karl Stenerud. tools/get_musashi.sh downloads it into third_party/musashi. The lockstep bench (tools/lockstep.sh) builds a
patched copy of it in build/musashi_gen (tools/musashi_patch.py); that copy is not distributed. The license text is in
Musashi's own readme.txt and in the header of m68kcpu.c.

SoftFloat, release 2b, by John R. Hauser, in the MAME packaging that is part of the Musashi tree
(third_party/musashi/softfloat). It is compiled into the lockstep bench. Its license (derivative works are allowed, also for
commercial purposes, if the source states that the work is derivative and keeps the four license paragraphs) is in the header
of each SoftFloat source file and in softfloat/README.txt.

Test data, downloaded and never shipped:
- SingleStepTests 680x0 (github.com/SingleStepTests/680x0), the 68000 set, fetched by tools/fetch_tests.sh.
- WinUAE (github.com/tonioni/WinUAE), the CPU tester of Toni Wilen and the WinUAE team, licensed under the GNU GPL. Cloned
  and built by tools/cputest_build.sh to generate the 68020 and 68882 test data. No WinUAE source is part of this repository.
  The 68881/68882 reference in sim/lockstep/fpu_ref.c was written from Motorola's manual; where the manual is silent it
  matches behavior measured with WinUAE's test data, and no WinUAE code or table was copied.

